          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first player to shed all cards from your hand in a round. The ultimate goal is to win the round and implement a rule that benefits you or hinders your rivals.',
          gameplay: 'On your turn, you must play a card that matches either the **Suit** or the **Rank** of the top card on the discard pile. If you cannot play, you must draw one card from the deck. If that card is playable, you may play it immediately.',
          keyRules: [
            'Match Suit or Rank.',
            "Call 'Bartok' on the penultimate card.",
            'Winner creates a new rule; rules stack session-wide.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Keep track of the rules! The most common way to lose is forgetting a rule that was made four rounds ago. In the early game, get rid of your high-point cards (Face cards).',
          intermediate: "Rule Synergies: If there's a rule that says 'The next player draws 2 on a 7', and you hold two 7s, try to hold them until the player to your left is low on cards.",
          advanced: "Rule Manipulation: When you win, create a rule that targets a specific card you know is gone from the deck or one that you personally have many of in the next hand (if you can predict the shuffle). Or, create a rule that is linguistically difficult ('Must speak only in rhymes on Clubs').",
          tips: [
            "Don't build too many 'Draw 2' rules, or the deck will run out before anyone can win.",
            "Assign one player as the 'Rule Keeper' to prevent arguments about the wording of old rules.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
